## 📊 **USE CASES / CASE STUDIES PAGE**

### **Headline:** "Real Problems. Real Solutions. Real Explanations."

### **Case Study 1: The VUS That Wasn't (Enhanced with SAE)**
- **Patient:** 62-year-old with metastatic colorectal cancer
- **Tempus Result:** VUS in APC intron, no actionable mutations
- **CrisPRO.ai Analysis:**
  - Evo 2 identified intronic mutation creates cryptic splice site
  - SAE Feature f1050 activated (splice acceptor site recognition)
  - Feature f24278 indicated mutation severity
  - Predicts APC haploinsufficiency
  - Boltz-2 models remaining APC protein function
- **Outcome:** Wnt pathway inhibitor recommended (off-label), patient responded
- **Impact:** "SAE features provided biological proof to justify off-label therapy"

### **NEW Case Study 5: Discovery Through Interpretability**
- **Company:** Academic cancer genomics lab
- **Challenge:** Thousands of noncoding mutations in whole genome sequencing data, no way to prioritize
- **CrisPRO.ai Solution:**
  - Ran Evo 2 + SAE analysis on entire cohort
  - Feature f19746 (prophage/mobile element) activated in 15% of tumors at novel loci
  - Further analysis revealed these were endogenous retroviral elements becoming active in cancer
  - SAE features guided discovery that traditional annotation missed
- **Outcome:** Published in high-impact journal, opened new therapeutic avenue
- **Impact:** "SAE interpretability turned data overload into biological discovery"

